<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<worksheet xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude" xml:id="activity_identify_der_graphs">
        <title>Identifying Graphs of Derivatives</title>
        <objectives>
                <ul>
                        <li>The learner will use connections between the shape of the graph of a function
and its derivative to discern which function could or could not be the
derivative of which.
                        </li>
                </ul>
        </objectives>
        <page>
        <exercise xml:id="fppfpf">
                <statement>
                        <figure xml:id="fig_fppfpf1">
                                <caption>The graphs <m>y=\ell(x)</m>, <m>y=M(x)</m>, and <m>y=k(x)</m>.</caption>
                                <image width="50%">
                                        <description>
                                                <p>
                                                        The graphs of three functions, l, M, and k, which are also f, f prime, and f double prime.
                                                </p>
                                        </description>
                                        <xi:include href="./fppfpf.xml"/>
                                </image>
                        </figure>
                        <p>
                                        The graphs of three functions are shown in <xref ref="fig_fppfpf1"/>. One of these graphs is <m>y=f(x)</m>, a second one is the graph of the derivative of <m>f(x)</m>, <m>y=f'(x)</m>. The third one is the graph of the derivative of <m>f'(x)</m>, <m>y=f''(x)</m>.
                        </p>
                        <p>
                                        Identify which of the graphs, green solid, blue dashed, or black dotted, is <m>f(x)</m>, which is <m>f'(x)</m>, and which is <m>f''(x)</m>.
                        </p>
                        <p>
                                Explain your choices clearly in terms of function values and rates of change or slopes!
                        </p>
                </statement>
        </exercise>
        </page>
        <page>
        <exercise xml:id="gppgpg">
                <statement>
                        <figure xml:id="fig_gppgpg1">
                                <caption>The graphs <m>y=h(x)</m>, <m>y=T(x)</m>, and <m>y=s(x)</m>.</caption>
                                <image width="50%">
                                        <description>
                                                <p>
                                                        The graphs of three functions, h, T, and s, which are also g, g prime, and g double prime.
                                                </p>
                                        </description>
                                        <xi:include href="./gppgpg.xml"/>
                                </image>
                        </figure>
                        <p>
                                        The graphs of three functions are shown in <xref ref="fig_fppfpf1"/>. One of these graphs is <m>y=g(x)</m>, a second one is the graph of the derivative of <m>g(x)</m>, <m>y=g'(x)</m>. The third one is the graph of the derivative of <m>g'(x)</m>, <m>y=g''(x)</m>.
                        </p>
                        <p>
                                        Identify which of the graphs, green solid, blue dashed, or black dotted, is <m>g(x)</m>, which is <m>g'(x)</m>, and which is <m>g''(x)</m>.
                        </p>
                        <p>
                                Explain your choices clearly in terms of function values and rates of change or slopes!
                        </p>
                </statement>
        </exercise>
</page>
</worksheet>
